From 66ccb42130a24ff972b76c81148263c428c37587 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:00:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] mm/nommu: handle PFN remap actions as identity mappings
To: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>,
    "Liam R. Howlett" <liam@infradead.org>,
    Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>,
    David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>,
    Jann Horn <jannh@google.com>,
    Pedro Falcato <pfalcato@suse.de>,
    Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>,
    Greg Ungerer <gerg@linux-m68k.org>,
    linux-mm@kvack.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

Since commit ab04945f91bc ("mm: update mem char driver to use
mmap_prepare"), the /dev/mem mmap_prepare hook sets an MMAP_REMAP_PFN
action for each mapping. The NOMMU versions of mmap_action_prepare() and
mmap_action_complete() both WARN for every action other than
MMAP_NOTHING, and mmap_action_complete() then returns -EINVAL, so on
NOMMU every /dev/mem mmap() fails after two WARNs:

  WARNING: mm/util.c:1614 at mmap_action_prepare+0x12/0x1e
  WARNING: mm/util.c:1636 at mmap_action_complete+0x38/0xe2

On NOMMU, a driver's get_unmapped_area() hook returns the physical
address of the range that the driver then remaps, so a direct mapping is
an identity mapping, and the NOMMU remap_pfn_range() returns success
only for an identity mapping. Add remap_pfn_range_prepare() with the
same check and the same VMA flags, call it and
io_remap_pfn_range_prepare() from mmap_action_prepare(), and complete a
prepared MMAP_REMAP_PFN action without further work.

A direct mapping of the last page of a 32-bit address space ends at
2^32, which wraps vm_end to zero. Fail such a mapping with -ENOMEM.

Reproduced on QEMU's riscv64 virt machine with nommu_virt_defconfig plus
CONFIG_DEVMEM=y and CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM=n: mapping offset 0x80000000 of
/dev/mem fails with the WARNs above; with this patch mmap() returns
0x80000000, and reading the mapping gives the kernel Image header.

Fixes: ab04945f91bc ("mm: update mem char driver to use mmap_prepare")
Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
 mm/nommu.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 mm/util.c  |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
index 6c6f953296..23a36fcc40 100644
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -1164,6 +1164,10 @@ unsigned long do_mmap(struct file *file,
 					goto error_just_free;
 
 				capabilities &= ~NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT;
+			} else if (addr > TASK_SIZE - len) {
+				/* The VMA end must not wrap past TASK_SIZE. */
+				ret = -ENOMEM;
+				goto error_just_free;
 			} else {
 				vma->vm_start = region->vm_start = addr;
 				vma->vm_end = region->vm_end = addr + len;
@@ -1628,6 +1632,20 @@ int remap_pfn_range(struct vm_area_struct *vma, unsigned long addr,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(remap_pfn_range);
 
+int remap_pfn_range_prepare(struct vm_area_desc *desc)
+{
+	const struct mmap_action *action = &desc->action;
+	const unsigned long start = action->remap.start;
+
+	/* The driver's get_unmapped_area() hook returned this address. */
+	if (start != (action->remap.start_pfn << PAGE_SHIFT) ||
+	    !range_in_vma_desc(desc, start, start + action->remap.size))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	vma_desc_set_flags_mask(desc, VMA_REMAP_FLAGS);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 int vm_iomap_memory(struct vm_area_struct *vma, phys_addr_t start, unsigned long len)
 {
 	unsigned long pfn = start >> PAGE_SHIFT;
diff --git a/mm/util.c b/mm/util.c
index 80f6c71484..2c3909ebf6 100644
--- a/mm/util.c
+++ b/mm/util.c
@@ -1607,7 +1607,9 @@ int mmap_action_prepare(struct vm_area_desc *desc)
 	case MMAP_NOTHING:
 		break;
 	case MMAP_REMAP_PFN:
+		return remap_pfn_range_prepare(desc);
 	case MMAP_IO_REMAP_PFN:
+		return io_remap_pfn_range_prepare(desc);
 	case MMAP_SIMPLE_IO_REMAP:
 	case MMAP_KERNEL_PAGES:
 	case MMAP_DISCONTIG_KERNEL_PAGES:
@@ -1627,8 +1629,9 @@ int mmap_action_complete(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 
 	switch (action->type) {
 	case MMAP_NOTHING:
-		break;
+	/* A prepared PFN mapping is already the identity mapping. */
 	case MMAP_REMAP_PFN:
+		break;
 	case MMAP_IO_REMAP_PFN:
 	case MMAP_SIMPLE_IO_REMAP:
 	case MMAP_KERNEL_PAGES:

